From 5be1a528be31babb8950da6039f628409bf421ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:40:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 107/270] ARM: start the second CPU of the NVIDIA Tegra 2

As Linux does: enable the snoop control unit of the Cortex-A9 MPCore, point
the EVP reset vector to the trampoline, then hold the CPU in reset, let the
flow controller go, clock it and release the reset.

With several CPUs the Tegra timer takes its events from the private timer
(TWD) of each CPU, as TMR1 and its interrupt are shared; the time still
comes from the global TIMERUS counter. The loader passes the private timer
and its calibrated frequency.
